      "TRANS\nWORL\nBOBE\nN54341 M\nTWA",
      "TWA-Trans World Airlines\nBoeing 727-231A\nOver 1800.727's have been produced, making it the world's\nselling jetliner. The majority are 727-200 \"stretch\"\nversions, 20 feet longer than the original model, and carrying\n30 or more additional passengers. TWA's first -231 entered\nservice in 1968.\nPublished by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188,\nBethel, Conn. 06801 U.S.A.\nB-050\n85933-D\npost card\nPhoto courtesy Trans- World Airlines\nN54341\nc/n 21628\n2002.113.490"
